meta {
  name: describe
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sites/{{site}}/apply
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "content.read",
    "params": { "describe": true }
  }
}

docs {
  # What the site holds, and what this seat may do there

  Answered by Tracy itself (not by the site's component). Start here: it tells you which
  content types and locales the site has and which actions your seat's role allows.

  Look for:
  - the content types and locales listed, which the other requests filter by;
  - what your role may read and write. A `403` with `TOOLSET_NOT_GRANTED` elsewhere means
    the role lacks that toolset, not that the request is wrong.

  `describe` is asked alone: adding any other parameter answers `400 CONTENT_BAD_QUERY`.
}
